From e61019bb4423fcb1eab72e508ab3bc0a205bfa9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:20:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Define libc++ availability and libc selection explicitly

Set the two undefined configuration values to their existing preprocessor value, zero. This preserves the selected runtime branches while removing Wundef diagnostics.

TDD: Clang 22.1.8 with -std=c++23 -Wall -Wextra -Wundef -Werror -fsyntax-only config_test.cc fails for both missing identifiers before the definitions (exit 1), then passes after them (exit 0). Logs: emitted-native-policy-bvz375/libcxx-config-{red,green}.log in the fork execution record. Maintained Bazel verification remains required.

Refs holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed#61
---
 third_party/v8/libcxx_config/__config_site | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/v8/libcxx_config/__config_site b/third_party/v8/libcxx_config/__config_site
index 1053f9fe4..d74792b04 100644
--- a/third_party/v8/libcxx_config/__config_site
+++ b/third_party/v8/libcxx_config/__config_site
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #define _LIBCPP_HAS_VENDOR_AVAILABILITY_ANNOTATIONS 0
+#define _LIBCPP_AVAILABILITY_MINIMUM_HEADER_VERSION 0
 #define _LIBCPP_HAS_FILESYSTEM 1
 #define _LIBCPP_HAS_RANDOM_DEVICE 1
 #define _LIBCPP_HAS_LOCALIZATION 1
@@ -45,6 +46,7 @@
 
 #define _LIBCPP_LIBC_PICOLIBC 0
 #define _LIBCPP_LIBC_NEWLIB 0
+#define _LIBCPP_LIBC_LLVM_LIBC 0
 
 #define _LIBCPP_NO_AUTO_LINK
 #define _LIBCPP_REMOVE_TRANSITIVE_INCLUDES
